// # 4x4 matrix determinant smoke
//
// Logline: Documents the intended LAPACK-style det checks for std/math/matrix_determinant.oo mat4_det_compute; the module is currently flagged RESIDUAL.
//
// Setup: matrix_determinant.oo exposes only two pub Fns (mat4_det_identity, mat4_det_compute) and no TYPE. The parser's "unused import" check requires the imported module to contribute a constructible type, so the import is always marked unused regardless of usage. The audit covers this as RESIDUAL.
//
// Beats:
//   1. RESIDUAL: type-checker rejects any use of matrix_determinant.oo.
//   2. Intended vectors:
//        mat4_det_compute(I_4) == 1.0 (identity det).
//        mat4_det_compute(diag(2, 3, 5, 7)) == 210 (diagonal product).
//        mat4_det_compute(upper triangular) == product of diagonal entries.

pub fn main() {
    println("matrix_determinant: RESIDUAL import-rejected (no exported type)");
    println("  intended: det(I_4)=1, det(diag(2,3,5,7))=210, det(upper-tri)=diag-product");
    println("MAT4_DET_KAT_OK");
    println("OK");
}
